  "id": "COMPOUND:24024 - PROTEIN:5866",
  "verbalization": "Callyspongenol B is implicated in the biological activity of NCI-H446 through a series of target relationships that suggest a potential mechanism of action. The evidence indicates that Callyspongenol B acts as a target for Raji cells, which are then targeted by multiple compounds, including Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and 5-Hydroxytryptophan monohydrate, dl-. These compounds, in turn, have a target relationship with NCI-H446, suggesting a possible pathway where Callyspongenol B may influence NCI-H446 through these intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Callyspongenol B in modulating NCI-H446 through a series of molecular interactions, possibly involving receptor or enzyme targeting. The evidence supports a mechanism where Callyspongenol B may act as a modulator or inhibitor of the downstream targets, which in turn affect NCI-H446. The relationship is supported by multiple independent pathways, though the exact mechanism of interaction between Callyspongenol B and NCI-H446 remains to be fully elucidated.",
